-fbffd53e9e1d" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283787 1034 "2" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283787 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534344 true] [17592186283787 1111 #uuid "25f7b36d-75ac-5ff3-8bdd-19a33789bd07" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283788 1034 "-3" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283788 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534344 true] [17592186283788 1111 #uuid "c430c6b6-fd74-5a80-980c-0a05cc31553e" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283789 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283790 13194139534344 true] [17592186283789 1089 "q-117010" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283789 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534344 true] [17592186283789 1100 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\n- $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$\n- $(0,0)$\n- $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283789 1113 #uuid "b17707f8-d0a8-5f70-818e-f01d27903349" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283789 1145 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(0,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,0)$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283791 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283792 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283793 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283794 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283795 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1041 "selection" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283792 13194139534344 true] [17592186283790 1110 #uuid "6e969b59-2bad-5cd6-8e50-dd623e3b7254" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283791 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283791 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534344 true] [17592186283791 1111 #uuid "874a00aa-7fa0-594c-a983-1d469c66e3d6" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283792 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534344 true] [17592186283792 1111 #uuid "61fc9906-f248-54b2-ac04-53f23ba7913d" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283793 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534344 true] [17592186283793 1111 #uuid "4501a453-79ed-547a-bf76-f82a63525114" 13194139534344 true] [17592186283794 1034 "I a